<http://data.silknow.org/object/313d4c07-d628-3318-8e57-dab42903a540>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Waistcoat from court suit. Cream ribbed silk embroidered with coloured silk threads, coloured glass paillettes in green, yellow, blue, amber, metal sequins and coiled wire. It is embroidered with a border of stylised floral sprays at the closing edges, hem and pocket-flaps. The front is embroidered all over with a sprig pattern. It has eleven embroidered buttons, the uppermost of which is non-functioning.\n\nIt is lined throughout with fustian with panels of silk at the lower-front and closing edges. The back is of fustian and has two pairs of cotton tapes to adjust fit."@en , "Waistcoat, ensemble with court suit (654&A-1898), embroidered silk, England,1800-1810"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/b048e8b3-971b-34c0-bbad-006a58352951> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Waistcoat, ensemble with court suit (654&A-1898), embroidered silk, England,1800-1810"@en , "Waistcoat from court suit. Cream ribbed silk embroidered with coloured silk threads, coloured glass paillettes in green, yellow, blue, amber, metal sequins and coiled wire. It is embroidered with a border of stylised floral sprays at the closing edges, hem and pocket-flaps. The front is embroidered all over with a sprig pattern. It has eleven embroidered buttons, the uppermost of which is non-functioning.\n\nIt is lined throughout with fustian with panels of silk at the lower-front and closing edges. The back is of fustian and has two pairs of cotton tapes to adjust fit."@en ;
